  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "htmlParseTryOrFinish",
    "file": "libxml2/HTMLparser.c",
    "description": "In the XML_PARSER_CONTENT state, htmlParseTryOrFinish iterates with `while (... && (in->cur < in->end))` but then unconditionally reads `cur = in->cur[0]` after calling htmlParseReference/htmlParseCharData. Those helpers can advance `in->cur` to `in->end`, so the post-call read dereferences one byte past the available buffer. With push parsing and terminate=1 on empty final chunk, this becomes a global OOB read on adjacent static data.",
    "conditions": "Triggered via fuzz/html.c push parser path: input is split into chunks, then `htmlParseChunk(ctxt, NULL, 0, 1)` calls htmlParseTryOrFinish with terminate=1. A crafted document (PoC includes malformed bytes/meta charset) drives parser into CONTENT loop where htmlParseCharData or htmlParseReference consumes the last byte and sets `in->cur == in->end`; the subsequent unconditional `in->cur[0]` read causes ASan global-buffer-overflow. Requires reaching CONTENT state with buffer boundary exactly exhausted inside that loop."
  },
